(OUT/'channel-research.json').write_text(json.dumps(outcome,indent=2)+'\n')
rows=[]
for n,c in enumerate(channels,1):
 uk=f"<small>UK estimate: {c['uk_visits']/1e6:,.2f}m</small>" if c.get('uk_visits') else '<small>UK share not established here</small>'
 rows.append(f"<tr><td>{n}. <strong>{e(c['name'])}</strong><small>{e(c['kind'])}</small></td><td><a href='{e(c['traffic'])}'>{c['visits']/1e6:,.2f}m</a>{uk}</td><td>{e(c['fees'])} <a href='{e(c['terms'])}'>Official terms</a></td><td>{e(c['fit'])}</td></tr>")
cards=''.join(f"<article><h3>{e(c['name'])}</h3><p>{e(c['action'])}</p></article>" for c in channels)
postcards=''.join(f"<article><h3>{e(p['title'])}</h3><p class='badge'>Prepared · not published</p><p class='caption'>{e(p['caption'])}</p><p><strong>Alt text:</strong> {e(p['alt_text'])}</p><small>Product SKU: {e(p['sku'])} · verified original {p['width']} × {p['height']} px</small></article>" for p in posts)
source_html=''.join(f"<li><a href='{e(url)}'>{e(name)}</a> — {e(note)}</li>" for name,url,note in sources)
source_html+=''.join(f"<li><a href='{e(c['traffic'])}'>{e(c['name'])} traffic</a> and <a href='{e(c['terms'])}'>official fee / programme terms</a>.</li>" for c in channels)
board=base64.b64encode((OUT/'instagram-review-contact-sheet.jpg').read_bytes()).decode()
doc=f"""<!doctype html><html lang='en'><meta charset='utf-8'><meta name='viewport' content='width=device-width,initial-scale=1'><title>Boldstone · Next sales channels · 7 November 2026</title>
<style>*{{box-sizing:border-box}}body{{margin:0;background:#f4f4f1;color:#202422;font:16px/1.6 system-ui,sans-serif}}main{{max-width:1180px;margin:auto;padding:44px 24px 80px}}h1{{font-size:clamp(30px,5vw,49px);line-height:1.15;max-width:900px}}h2{{font-size:27px;margin-top:45px}}h3{{font-size:20px;margin-top:0}}a{{color:#255568;text-underline-offset:3px}}nav{{display:flex;gap:22px;flex-wrap:wrap;border-block:1px solid #c8ceca;padding:15px 0}}.eyebrow,small{{font-size:13px;color:#56605a}}small{{display:block}}.lead{{font-size:20px;max-width:900px}}.note{{border-left:4px solid #856738;padding:12px 20px;background:#f0e8dc}}.grid{{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(275px,1fr));gap:16px}}article{{background:white;padding:24px;border:1px solid #d5dad6;border-radius:9px}}.table-wrap{{overflow:auto}}table{{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;background:white;font-size:14px;min-width:850px}}td,th{{text-align:left;padding:18px 14px;vertical-align:top;border-bottom:1px solid #d5dad6}}th{{background:#e3e8e3}}td:first-child{{min-width:185px}}td:nth-child(2){{min-width:130px}}.badge{{display:inline-block;background:#eee3cd;color:#67491b;padding:4px 10px;border-radius:4px;font-size:13px}}.caption{{white-space:pre-wrap;font-size:15px}}img{{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;margin:20px 0}}li{{margin:10px 0}}footer{{margin-top:45px;border-top:1px solid #c8ceca;padding-top:20px}}@media print{{body{{background:white}}main{{max-width:none;padding:0}}nav{{display:none}}article{{break-inside:avoid}}table{{min-width:0;font-size:11px}}a{{color:inherit}}}}</style>
<main><p class='eyebrow'>BOLDSTONE SCULPTURE · 7 NOVEMBER 2026</p><h1>Where to list next without an upfront fee</h1><p class='lead'>Prioritise Pinterest for product discovery and test Whatnot with smaller, safely packed works. Amazon Individual has the largest UK shopping audience in this comparison, but shipping economics and onboarding still need checking.</p>
<nav><a href='#overview'>Overview</a><a href='#competitors'>Channel comparison</a><a href='#guidance'>Guidance</a><a href='#posts'>Five prepared posts</a><a href='#sources'>Sources</a></nav>
<section id='overview'><h2>Overview</h2><p>Your three files contain 263 selling routes, 168 directory routes and 12 held/excluded entries, with substantial overlap between files. These have been reconciled into 443 distinct numbered entries. This report compares selected higher-traffic candidates; it is not a fresh fee-and-eligibility audit of all 443.</p><p>The seller baseline is the existing 176-product publication catalogue, drawn from 181 retained component records. Product descriptions must use the current gypsum-based material wording, identify decorative effects as finishes, disclose handmade pattern variation, and keep companion pieces and Sally Price commissions clear.</p><p class='note'><strong>Not yet published:</strong> five additional Instagram posts are prepared below. Another Chrome task is switching windows, so no publication is counted until the exact account, image, caption and product tag can be saved and read back safely.</p><div class='grid'><article><h3>Faire and Furnitures</h3><p>Last verified on 7 November: 176 Faire price records and 176 Furnitures live products. Faire requires an owner GBP payout-bank action. Furnitures states Stripe payouts arrive in a future release; its fixed delivery policy remains a commercial limitation. No new checkout or payout success is asserted.</p></article><article><h3>Saatchi price correction</h3><p>Bone Spiral I was saved at US$307. The last independently verified Ammonite Petite II price is US$138; US$265 is the intended correction. Saatchi explicitly rejected the prior save with a reCAPTCHA verification failure. The price must be freshly checked in the exact existing artwork before any new save; do not create a duplicate listing.</p></article></div></section>
<section id='competitors'><h2>Channel comparison</h2><p><strong>Traffic basis:</strong> September 2026 Semrush estimated worldwide website visits, all devices. These are neither unique people nor art buyers, and exclude unmeasured in-app activity. All five rows use the same metric and month. UK estimates are shown only where directly available.</p><div class='table-wrap'><table><thead><tr><th>Selected route</th><th>Monthly visits</th><th>Upfront and sale fees</th><th>Fit and limits</th></tr></thead><tbody>{''.join(rows)}</tbody></table></div><p><strong>Art-specific alternative:</strong> ArtMajeur advertises free unlimited listings and a 35% free-account commission, with about 0.89m September website visits. It is smaller than the five rows above but more directly aligned with sculptures. Verify original/edition eligibility and price recovery before using it. <a href='https://www.artmajeur.com/en/artmajeur-for-artists'>Official seller route</a> · <a href='https://es.semrush.com/website/artmajeur.com/overview/'>Traffic estimate</a>.</p></section>
<section id='guidance'><h2>Guidance</h2><div class='grid'>{cards}</div><h3>What not to overclaim</h3><ul><li>No upfront fee does not mean no commission, payment charge, VAT, packaging or delivery cost.</li><li>Amazon Handmade is not strictly zero-upfront: its official page waives the Professional subscription after the first month. Use the Individual route only if it supports the required category and fulfilment.</li><li>Do not infer marketplace conversion or UK demand from whole-domain traffic. Behance is an enquiry/portfolio route, not a physical-art checkout.</li><li>Do not register another Boldstone account where one already exists. The existing status notes identify several open applications and paid or conditional routes.</li><li>Do not copy Saatchi-only edition caps to other channels. Do not claim all 176 products meet an auction expert's acceptance or a carrier's packed-size limit.</li><li>Maintain genuine website/RRP consistency. Keep recorded actual Faire prices separate from profit-protection proposals, rather than inflating an unsupported reference retail price.</li></ul><p>Recommended sequence: establish the Pinterest catalogue route, verify a small Whatnot pilot, then assess ArtMajeur and Amazon Individual on their remaining account, photography and shipping requirements. Use Catawiki only for a suitable reviewed subset.</p></section>
<section id='posts'><h2>Five prepared Instagram posts</h2><p>Selected Dropbox originals were downloaded once for publishing and checked against native file IDs, revisions and content hashes. The images fit the posting aspect-ratio range without cropping. App purposes and primary choices were not changed. The tall Azure candidates were replaced by Bone Water Spiral to preserve the full artwork.</p><img src='data:image/jpeg;base64,{board}' alt='Review sheet showing the five selected sculpture photographs'><div class='grid'>{postcards}</div></section>
<section id='sources'><h2>Sources and evidence limits</h2><ul>{source_html}</ul><p>The controlling internal sources are the three supplied 6 November lists, the saved local Specifications snapshot, the current master workbook and the dated native publication receipts. External fee rules were checked on 7 November. The selected comparison uses public official programme/help pages and the traffic provider's own reports.</p><p>Knowledge and files were supplied directly. CRM, internal messaging and meeting transcripts are not relevant to this marketplace comparison. No extra provider installation is required. Fresh native account checks and the HTML browser preview await an uninterrupted browser window; structural readback is complete.</p></section><footer><small>Prepared {e(stamp)}. Research and local preparation only: no new accounts, subscriptions or paid promotions were activated.</small></footer></main></html>"""
